description:
Apply pending project C# changes through compilation and domain reload, and wait for the result. Use for changes requiring a full compile, refreshed test discovery, serialization/Inspector changes, or convergence after a burst of hot edits. Already-applied runtime changes can be observed before convergence. Requires the connected Editor to be in Edit Mode.

{optional_capability_guidance}

The result's status, compilation/reload/bridge state, phase, and recommended action determine the next step. `already_converged` means an in-progress compile applied the changes; `up_to_date` means assemblies were current; `reloaded_without_compile` also clears live hot-patch detours. Recovery or incomplete statuses require following their reported action. This brings the Editor forward and may take 10-60 seconds. Plan mode blocks this state-changing operation.
